Analysis only, NOT applied by build-hakios-metal.sh (darwin-lisa session 13, 2026-11-16): what ir3 makes of each
CoreAnimation pipeline a log names. Applies over the hakios-metal-*.patch series in userland/ (in a copy of
hakios-metal), then `make sweep MESA=1 MESA_HOST=.../build/mesa-host HAKIOS=..`.

- tools/sweep.cpp: with SWEEP_LISTING=FILE, `sweep -f FUNCTION -c I=V...` writes the stage's ir3 listing there.
- src/compiler.cpp: the listing ends with "; STATS waves=.. double=.. max_reg=.. prefetch=.. instrs=.. tex=.. preamble=..";
  HM_NOBIAS=1 drops a txb's bias before ir3 (to see whether the sample would then be prefetched: it is not, the
  coordinate is a noperspective varying, which ir3 25.0.7 never prefetches).

tools/ir3-survey.py LOG... runs it over every (fragment function, constants) the logs' "linked" lines name.

